// A reactive `for` that sends whole numbers to other entities, in rounds
// (Inputs/reactive_sends.ent): 100,000 things in a line, each telling
// the next when its number changes, which takes the greater. The sends
// come to the same in any order, so the `for` goes through the log of
// what changed and not through every thing; after 40 rounds a change has
// gone 40 places down the line. The same on one core and on all.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/reactive_sends.ent 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/reactive_sends.ent 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s

// CHECK:      5
// CHECK-NEXT: 5
// CHECK-NEXT: 9
// CHECK-NEXT: 5
// CHECK-NEXT: 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 40 rounds
